    {
      "text": "It freezes foes with an icy breath nearly -60 degrees Fahrenheit. What seems to be its body is actually hollow.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "Legends in snowy regions say that a woman who was lost on an icy mountain was reborn as Froslass.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "It freezes foes with an icy breath nearly -60 degrees Fahrenheit. What seems to be its body is actually hollow.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Legends in snowy regions say that a woman who was lost on an icy mountain was reborn as Froslass.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "When it finds humans or Pokémon it likes, it freezes them and takes them to its chilly den, where they become decorations.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "The soul of a woman lost on a snowy mountain possessed an icicle, becoming this Pokémon. The food it most relishes is the souls of men.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "It freezes hikers who have come to climb snowy mountains and carries them back to its home. It only goes after men it thinks are handsome.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "It’s said that on nights of terrible blizzards, it comes down to human settlements. If you hear it knocking at your door, do not open it!",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "After a woman met her end on a snowy mountain, her regrets lingered on. From them, this Pokémon was born. Its favorite food is frozen souls.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "It spits out cold air of nearly −60 degrees Fahrenheit to freeze its quarry. It brings frozen prey back to its lair and neatly lines them up.",
      "version": "shield"
    },
    {
      "text": "A Pokémon inhabited by the soul of a woman who died bearing a grudge in the snowy mountains. Legends of Froslass placing deathly curses on misbehaving men send shivers down my spine.",
      "version": "legends-arceus"
    }
  ],
